kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[2]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  modify_requirement,tt05,"portable-pty-e2e-primary","End-to-end TUI tests MUST use portable-pty as the primary integration driver: spawn the real binary as a PTY child, inject key sequences via the writer handle (with explicit sleep between keys when timing matters), read the raw byte stream from the reader handle, feed it to the existing VirtualTerminal (vte-based cell-grid parser), and assert on the resulting grid (cell content, SGR styles, cursor position). The PTY driver MUST support selecting which example or binary surface to spawn so smoke tests can follow the package's single primary example surface. This layer MUST cover crossterm's real event parsing of multi-byte sequences (Ctrl+arrow, Alt+arrow, bracketed paste markers) that cannot be exercised through in-process handle_input alone. portable-pty tests live in the workspace-level tests/tui_e2e/ directory (not packages/xylitol-tui/tests/) because they test the assembled binary, not the crate.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tt07,"single-primary-example-surface","The xylitol-tui package MUST keep a single primary example surface representing the fake coding-agent workflow rather than multiple overlapping showcase demos. Acceptance and E2E tests MUST target that primary example. The primary example MUST cover transcript history, tool activity, a sidebar or status surface, and an editable input area, and it MUST survive a realistic submit flow without violating the engine width contract.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[3]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tt05,"spawn-primary-example","the PTY E2E layer is asked to spawn agent_demo","the child process starts under portable-pty","the requested example launches and can be driven with the common send_keys and wait_for helpers"
  tt07,"agent-demo-submit-flow","the fake coding-agent example is mounted in-process at a representative terminal width","the test submits the default editor content","the render succeeds without a RenderError and the tool-running state becomes visible"
  tt07,"agent-demo-pty-smoke","the fake coding-agent example runs under portable-pty","the submit flow is driven through real terminal input","the process stays alive and the screen remains populated after submission"
